WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.140
Safeguards Rule implementation begins with scope: the institution's activities, customer relationships, customer information, and connected systems.

2
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:17.560
The resulting written program must be risk-based, proportional, and capable of protecting confidentiality, integrity, and availability.

3
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:26.220
A Qualified Individual supervises it, but accountability remains with the financial institution even when affiliates or service providers perform substantial work.

4
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.500
Safeguards must connect identified risk to operating evidence.

5
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:44.920
Access control, encryption, application security, multi-factor authentication, retention, disposal, change management, logging, testing, training, and provider oversight are continuing processes.

6
00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.420
Security events require prepared response and documentation.

7
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:57.040
Notification events require a separate analysis of acquisition, encryption status, consumer count, discovery, and timing.

8
00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:03.300
The fewer-than-five-thousand-consumers provision limits four requirements; it does not erase the program.

9
00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.140
Operationally, use eight actions.

10
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.520
Confirm scope.

11
00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.420
Inventory customer information.

12
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.880
Assess risk.

13
00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:13.340
Implement safeguards.

14
00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.440
Test and monitor.

15
00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.700
Govern providers and personnel.

16
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.760
Prepare for incidents and notification.

17
00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.820
Preserve evidence and improve the program.

18
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:31.460
Compliance depends on coordinated legal, governance, security, privacy, procurement, and operational judgment.

19
00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:38.600
Regulatory text controls; guidance helps with interpretation; technical standards support implementation.

20
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.220
None replaces the others.

21
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.120
The durable objective is not a one-time checklist or an audit-day collection of documents.

22
00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:54.980
It is a maintained information security program that can explain its scope, decisions, performance, failures, and improvements with evidence across every operating period.
